00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:25.680
- To all my non-Black allies:

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.130
When you get in those positions of power,

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.260
use your privilege to help break down

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.697
this systematic racial--

00:05:33.697 --> 00:05:37.625
(crowd cheering drowns out speaker)

00:05:37.625 --> 00:05:39.187
- Can everybody please record this?

00:05:39.187 --> 00:05:42.500
I have a message for my preschool teacher.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.050
He was pretty racist towards me.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:47.170
I was one of the only
Black kids at my preschool,

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:50.170
and he used to call me in
randomly into his office,

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:53.940
and he made me stand in the
corner, by myself, for hours.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.090
I'm talking hours by myself!

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.580
But guess what?

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.643
I'm still here standing today.

00:06:00.643 --> 00:06:03.389
I'm still here!
- [Crowd] (cheers)

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:04.750
- I'm still here!

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:07.140
All those countless hours,
man, my legs are strong.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:07.973
I'm still standing.

00:06:07.973 --> 00:06:09.060
- [Woman] What's his name?

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.190
- Mr. Layman.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.289
Mr. Layman, if you can hear me--

00:06:11.289 --> 00:06:12.122
- [Man] Fuck you, Mr. Layman!

00:06:12.122 --> 00:06:15.030
- I'm still here!
- [Crowd] (cheers)

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:18.230
- Every single situation
that I was in as a kid,

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.820
it was always blamed on me and my brother

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.670
because we were the only Black
kids in our neighborhood.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.010
So we were always the
ones that were blamed on

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:27.054
and put on with all this shit,

00:06:27.054 --> 00:06:28.397
and I'm so tired of just seeing

00:06:28.397 --> 00:06:30.770
all this fucking negativity on the news.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.620
All this shit, and nothing's
fucking being done with it!

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.530
I wanna yell this at the cops, too.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.494
We want fucking change!

00:06:37.494 --> 00:06:41.263
- Stand up to your friends
that don't think it's right!

00:06:41.263 --> 00:06:43.881
Stand up to your families!

00:06:43.881 --> 00:06:46.777
History has repeated itself over and over

00:06:46.777 --> 00:06:49.710
and over again that good will win!

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.270
Please keep going.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.840
Do not give up.

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:55.800
When you think it is over, it is not!

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.280
- I basically want people to know

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:02.280
that it's not just from
being shot in the street

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.410
because you're Black and brown.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.740
It goes further than that, okay?

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.960
We've been dealing with this for too long

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.840
where nothing could change, okay?

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.820
It's hard for my people to
get jobs over other folks,

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:17.590
it's hard for us to get loans,

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:20.210
and I'm talking about
school loans, house loans,

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.440
like all the way across the board, okay?

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.140
I want people to wake up.

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:28.390
Wake up, and realize that it
takes everybody being together.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.660
It takes not just us trying to stand up,

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:33.600
but it takes the White
folks, it takes the Italians,

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.690
it takes the Asians!

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:37.220
It takes everybody that's
in this melting pot,

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.560
everybody to come together
and make this thing good.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.960
I mean, I've got a million and one times

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:47.520
where I've been treated funny
just because of who I am.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:50.820
But I'm a military veteran,
I'm a college graduate,

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:54.450
and y'know, I'm nonviolent,
and I love people,

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.820
and I'm just trying to
really get a better message

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.280
so that way we can elevate the humankind

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.250
to the next level instead of just

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.380
running around like rats
like we've been doing.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:04.220
- I mean, I don't get it.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:06.810
They're murdering us, then
telling us to be quiet

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:08.280
about them killing us.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.560
It comes to a point in time

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.260
where you have to stop
caring about skin color

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:15.030
and start caring about
the war that we are in.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.360
I know a lot of people don't want to think

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:19.210
that it's a war, but look around you.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:21.630
Look at the riots that's
happening across the country now.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:23.840
It is becoming a war, and yes,

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.610
you're gonna have to
fight for your freedom.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.620
We're not special.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:29.360
Like any other countries that you see

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.640
that are tired of their
governments, what do they do?

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.220
They turn around and they fight,

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.830
they fight for their fucking lives.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:39.400
I think Americans, Black,
White, Hispanic, whatever,

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:42.190
are starting to see that there
is no other choice coming

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.800
but to fight for your lives.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.200
We're being peaceful out
here, and in a couple of hours

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.150
they're going to send the bean bags,

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.410
they're gonna send the tear gas,

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.050
and they're gonna shoot
at us for being peaceful.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:57.050
So if you don't see how that
is ridiculous, then you sleep!

00:08:57.250 --> 00:09:01.340
And, I mean, keep sleeping
until everybody dead.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:02.410
That's it, thank you.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.557
- The overall message
that I want to send is

00:09:04.557 --> 00:09:06.077
"Stop killing us.

00:09:06.077 --> 00:09:07.460
"Just stop."

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.700
That's all I wanna say,
is just fucking stop.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:13.740
- I'd rather die by the Coronavirus

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.340
than die at the hands of police.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.410
- I'm Black, I matter, and I'm trans.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.733
I fear for my life every
day, but I'm out here

00:09:21.733 --> 00:09:23.170
and I'm here with you guys.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.480
Black lives matter, all lives matter,

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.900
and trans lives matter as well.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:31.266
- We're not trying to riot,
but rioting is just like,

00:09:31.266 --> 00:09:33.370
the process of what we're getting through

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.130
and what we're going
through, rioting happened.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.240
Like, we're not here to
riot and we're not here

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:40.750
to break stuff, but people
are so angry and like,

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:41.583
this has been going on for years

00:09:41.583 --> 00:09:43.810
that this just happened, y'know.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.520
- I want people to know that
being oppressed for 400 years

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:49.500
does something to people,
no matter who you are,

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.180
and the fact that people are just focusing

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.310
on the buildings being destroyed

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:54.360
instead of the Black
lives that have been lost

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.540
is just kind of sickening.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.020
Cause like, you can't bring back a life

00:09:57.020 --> 00:10:00.570
but you can rebuild a building,
and America needs to wake up

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.710
and see this is not for anything.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.420
Black people are trying
to get a message out

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.530
for people to be heard,
because peaceful protesting.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:08.850
We've been doing that for years
and they haven't heard us,

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.780
but now they're hearing us
because we're making some noise.

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:13.437
- People ask me, like,

00:10:13.437 --> 00:10:15.193
"What do you think needs to change?

00:10:16.067 --> 00:10:18.300
"Why does this keep on happening?"

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.650
And I know it keeps happening

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.020
because when you look at any thing,

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:27.460
person, animal, as lesser than you,

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:30.990
it's easy to treat them as such.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:33.550
So I'm mixed, I'm half Black, half White.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:36.320
One time, I was in Columbus, Ohio.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.930
It was me, my brother,
and my cousin who's Black.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:43.420
I just so happened to have
the hoodie on that day,

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.480
and we were walking in a mall.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:49.880
And as we were walking, I
didn't know there were police

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:50.713
at the time, say

00:10:50.713 --> 00:10:51.830
"Hey, get against the wall!"

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:52.663
I'm like,

00:10:52.663 --> 00:10:53.660
"No, why would I get against the wall?"

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.670
and tried to walk around them.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.320
They threw me to the ground.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.880
My cousin jumped in, they
beat him up pretty bad.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.960
I didn't know how that
affected me as a child

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:05.510
because I was 13, but as I get
older and seeing these things

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.680
keep on happen over and over again,

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.380
it made me realize that me,

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:11.980
someone who's not dark-skinned,
I can only imagine

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.530
if I was a dark-skinned
Black person how they have

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:17.160
to navigate through this
world and get profiled.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.050
I think it's just really important for us

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:23.640
to educate ourselves on
things that aren't so surface.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:26.490
Ask the hard questions of why things are

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.560
the way that they are.

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.100
- I'm out here for Black Lives Matter

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.440
and Trans Lives Matter, and
it's really important to me

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.960
because I'm also part
of the LGBTQ community

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.050
and we've also been getting hurt

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:38.600
by a lot of the police brutality
that has been going on.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.503
- I just really can't
even believe the fact

00:11:40.503 --> 00:11:42.550
that just a week ago, or
a couple of weeks ago,

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.540
you had people protesting
the quarantine wearing a mask

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.860
because they wanted a haircut,
with full armed rifles,

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:50.590
guns with loaded ammunition,
but we're out here

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:53.190
protesting peacefully,
but people want to gas us

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.210
and make it violent and
all that extra stuff

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:56.150
that's just not needed.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.300
One of the main reasons that
I'm out here is for my brother.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:11:59.840
My brother doesn't get
the same privilege as me.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.700
I'm Black and I'm a
female, my brother is Black

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:05.090
and he's a male, and he faces
stereotyping and all that,

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:06.290
especially because he has tattoos,

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.110
so his life is 10 times
more harder than me.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:09.820
He gets profiled, and
when he leaves the house,

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:12.340
I'm not sure if he's coming
home to us in one piece.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.200
We never know.

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:14.760
So, that's why I'm out here.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.110
- We are tired.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.930
We are exhausted that
we even have to protest

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.683
during a global pandemic.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:24.970
We just want peace, and
we just want justice.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:28.300
That's all we want, and
that's all we've ever wanted.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:31.580
There are people who are
taking these protests

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.900
as chances to live out
their riot fantasies,

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.530
but this isn't what we're about.

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:40.360
We're about peace, and
we just want justice

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.540
for everyone who has died mercilessly.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:44.700
- We just want to let you guys know

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.773
that silence speaks volumes.

00:12:55.935 --> 00:12:56.873
- [Woman With Cap] No justice!

00:12:56.873 --> 00:12:57.706
- [Crowd] No peace!

00:12:57.706 --> 00:12:58.547
- [Woman With Cap] No racist!

00:12:58.547 --> 00:12:59.430
- [Crowd] Police!

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:00.434
Say his name!

00:13:00.434 --> 00:13:01.387
- [Crowd] George Floyd!

00:13:01.387 --> 00:13:02.228
Say his name!

00:13:02.228 --> 00:13:03.151
- [Crowd] George Floyd!

00:13:03.151 --> 00:13:04.008
- [Woman with Cap] Say his name!

00:13:04.008 --> 00:13:04.917
- [Crowd] George Floyd!

00:13:04.917 --> 00:13:05.792
- [Woman with Cap] Say his name!

00:13:05.792 --> 00:13:07.709
- [Crowd] George Floyd!

